issue_context.body:
`LastValue`, which is used by `ObservableGauge<>`, has an `Update(double value)` method that just does:
```C#
        private double? _lastValue;

        public override void Update(double value)
        {
            _lastValue = value;
        }
```
Writing a `double` on a 32-bit platform is not guaranteed to be an atomic operation, and regardless of bitness, writing a `double?` is not guaranteed to be an atomic operation. We could thus end up in a situation where, for example, `_lastValue` reports it contains a value but the value hasn't actually been initialized, or where the reported value is an amalgum of an old value and one currently being written.

