Could this be enabling all metrics in a process that was otherwise subscribed to none?

I added a simple
```c#
var meter = new Meter("TestMeter");
var testCounter = meter.CreateCounter<int>("test.testCounter");

_ = Task.Run(async () =>
{
    while (true)
    {
        await Task.Delay(1000);
        Console.WriteLine($"Enabled: {testCounter.Enabled}");
    }
});
```

into the benchmark project in question and it appears to be enabled after this change.

Previously my understanding was that one of Blanch's changes during Preview7 had regressed this behavior and @tarekgh's change here was intended to restore the previous .NET 8 behavior. However doing some testing now, thats not what I see. What I see in my test for .NET 8 is omitting the Metrics argument did not enable any metrics.

We probably need to dig deeper and make sure we understand exactly what happened, but now it looks like this change that was intended to re-align us to .NET 8 behavior instead changed us away from .NET 8 behavior. This is my test case:

```C#
internal class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        Meter m = new Meter("MyMeter");
        m.CreateObservableCounter("MyCounter", () => 1);
        MyEventListener listener = new MyEventListener();
        Console.ReadLine();
    }
}

class MyEventListener : EventListener
{
    protected override void OnEventSourceCreated(EventSource eventSource)
    {
        Console.WriteLine(eventSource.Name);
        if(eventSource.Name == "System.Diagnostics.Metrics")
        {
            EnableEvents(eventSource, EventLevel.Informational, (EventKeywords)0x7/*, new Dictionary<string,string?>() { { "Metrics", "MyMeter" } }*/);
        }
    }

    protected override void OnEventWritten(EventWrittenEventArgs eventData)
    {
        if(eventData.EventSource.Name == "System.Runtime")
        {
            return;
        }
        Console.WriteLine(eventData.EventName);
        for (int i = 0; i < eventData.Payload.Count; i++)
        {
            Console.WriteLine($"\t{eventData.PayloadNames[i]}: {eventData.Payload[i]}");
        }
    }
}
```
